### Run only relevant tests per mutant

Source: https://github.com/infection/infection/blob/master/src/TestFramework/PhpUnit/Config/Builder/MutationConfigBuilder.php

When testing each mutant, Infection rebuilds phpunit.xml to include only the specific test files that cover the mutated line. The existing test suite is removed entirely, and a new suite is created with just those test file paths. This avoids running the full test suite for every mutant.

```php
private function setFilteredTestsToRun(array $tests, SafeDOMXPath $xPath): void
{
    $this->removeExistingTestSuite($xPath);

    $this->addTestSuiteWithFilteredTestFiles($tests, $xPath);
}

private function addTestSuiteWithFilteredTestFiles(
    array $tests,
    SafeDOMXPath $xPath,
): void {
    $nodeToAppendTestSuite = $xPath->queryElement('/phpunit/testsuites');

    $nodeToAppendTestSuite ??= $xPath->queryElement('/phpunit');

    $testSuite = $xPath->document->createElement('testsuite');
    $testSuite->setAttribute('name', 'Infection testsuite with filtered tests');

    $orderedTestFilePaths = $this->testRunOrderResolver->resolve($tests);

    foreach ($orderedTestFilePaths as $testFilePath) {
        $fileElement = $xPath->document->createElement('file', $testFilePath);

        $testSuite->appendChild($fileElement);
    }

    Assert::isInstanceOf($nodeToAppendTestSuite, DOMNode::class);

    $nodeToAppendTestSuite->appendChild($testSuite);
}
```

--------------------------------

### Mutate only covered source files

Source: https://github.com/infection/infection/blob/master/src/Mutation/FileMutationGenerator.php

When `onlyCovered` is true and a source file has no covering tests at all, the generator yields zero mutations for that file — skipping it entirely. This is how Infection restricts mutation to only covered source files. Combined with `--git-diff-base` (changed files only), selective mutation is achieved.

```php
public function generate(
    SplFileInfo $sourceFile,
    bool $onlyCovered,
    array $mutators,
): iterable {
    Assert::allIsInstanceOf($mutators, Mutator::class);

    $trace = $this->trace($sourceFile);

    if ($onlyCovered && !$trace->hasTests()) {
        return;
    }

    [$initialStatements, $originalFileTokens] = $this->createAst(
        $sourceFile,
        $trace,
    );

    yield from $this->generateMutations(
        $mutators,
        $sourceFile,
```

### Nomenclature > M

Source: https://github.com/infection/infection/blob/master/doc/nomenclature.md

Mutation Analysis is the core testing cycle consisting of generation, filtering, materialisation, and evaluation. Materialisation involves writing mutated code to disk and spawning an isolated process, while evaluation executes tests against the mutant to record outcomes.

--------------------------------

### The execution pipeline > AST parsing to Mutant evaluation

Source: https://github.com/infection/infection/blob/master/AGENTS.md

AST parsing labels code eligibility and connects structural elements, while mutation generation creates potential code changes. These mutants are materialized and evaluated in parallel processes, with escaped mutants potentially undergoing additional static analysis via PHPStan or Mago adapters.

